  Agdagen is a compiler backend to translate OCaml files into Agda. The
original project to which it was added is coqgen, which was making the
translation of OCaml into Coq. The scripts below should work for both.
  Let's call OCAML_PATH the absolute path to the ocaml folder on your computer,
the root folder of both projects.
  The first time you install agdagen, assuming you are in <OCAML_PATH> and coqc
is in your path, you will need to do, in the following order:

$> ./configure
$> make core
$> coqc -R testsuite/tests/coqgen coqgen testsuite/tests/coqgen/coqgen_defs.v

Then, if you have a "test.ml" file that you want to translate, you can either :
 - put it in testsuite/tests/coqgen and run
  $> ./boot/ocamlrun ./ocamlc -I stdlib -c -coq testsuite/tests/coqgen/test.ml
to generate a test.v file (in testsuite/tests/coqgen) that you can then run;
 - put it in testsuite/tests/agdagen and run
  $> ./boot/ocamlrun ./ocamlc -I stdlib -c -agda testsuite/tests/agdagen/test.ml
to generate a test.agda file (in testsuite/tests/agdagen) that you can then run;

  Here are some bash scripts to make the use of coqgen and agdagen easier. You
can for instance add them to your .bashrc (don't forget to change OCAML_PATH by
its actual value).

++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
run() { oo=<OCAML_PATH>
        if [ "$1" == agda ]; then
                ext=agda
        else
                ext=v
        fi
        echo Running the command
        echo .../ocaml/boot/ocamlrun .../ocaml/ocamlc -I .../ocaml/stdlib -c -"$1" .../ocaml/testsuite/tests/"$1"gen/"$2".ml
        echo cat .../ocaml/testsuite/tests/"$1"gen/"$2"."$ext"

        if "$oo"/boot/ocamlrun "$oo"/ocamlc -I "$oo"/stdlib -c -"$1" "$oo"/testsuite/tests/"$1"gen/"$2".ml ; then
            cat "$oo"/testsuite/tests/"$1"gen/"$2"."$ext";
        fi }
++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
out() { oo=<OCAML_PATH>
        if [ "$1" == agda ]; then
                ext=agda
        else
                ext=v
        fi
        emacs "$oo"/testsuite/tests/"$1"gen/"$2"."$ext"; }
++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++

To translate a .ml file, run:
$> run <1> <2>

To display the generated code:
$> out <1> <2>

<1> : agda / coq
<2> : name of the .ml file (without the extension)

Example: "Translate "example.ml" to Agda and display the generated code"
$> run agda example
$> out example
